{% extends "tutorial_base.html.j2" %}

{% block tutorial_body %}
        <!-- Intro Card -->
        <div class="doc-intro-card">
          <h2>Heavy-Plate Piercing, Open-Path Kerf, Clean Remnants &amp; Zero Torch Dives</h2>
          <p>
            Thick plate, open trim cuts, and tight nests punish basic 2D CAM. Blowback wrecks nozzles on 1/2&Prime; steel, crossing an old kerf makes THC dive into the slats, and jagged skeletons waste half your sheet. Use these four tools to save your consumables and get more parts from every plate.
          </p>
          <div class="doc-intro-grid">
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Void Crash Guard</span>
              <span class="value">0.5 &times; Kerf + 4.0 mm THC Lock</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Open &amp; Thick Plate</span>
              <span class="value">L/R/Center Kerf + Edge-Start</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Pro Sheet Pack</span>
              <span class="value">Guillotine Crop + Chain/Bridge</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 1
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-1">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 01</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Void THC Auto-Lock (Zero Torch Dives)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              When your torch crosses an old kerf slot or pierce crater, arc voltage spikes and makes THC dive the torch straight into the slats.
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Every cut kerf and pierce crater is tracked automatically across flat-sheet and rotary jobs.</li>
              <li>When a later cut, common-line pass, or crop line comes within <code class="mono">0.5 &times; kerf width + 4.0 mm</code> of a void, your <code class="mono">G1</code> move splits automatically.</li>
              <li>THC locks across the gap and unlocks once your torch clears back onto solid steel. No manual keep-out rules needed.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 2
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-2">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 02</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Open-Path <code class="mono">Center / Left / Right</code> Kerf &amp; Thick-Plate <code class="mono">Edge-Start</code> (<code class="mono">Maker</code> &amp; <code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Set both options right inside the Features table for each contour:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li><strong>Open-Path Kerf (<code class="mono">Center (On-Line)</code> / <code class="mono">Left</code> / <code class="mono">Right</code>):</strong> Appears inline on open DXF or SVG slit and trim lines. Offset stays locked to the drawing stroke direction so trimmed edges hit exact size.</li>
              <li><strong><code class="mono">Edge-Start (Thick Plate)</code> Lead-In:</strong> Pick it in the <code class="mono">Lead-In Strategy</code> dropdown. You get an <code class="mono">Edge Overhang</code> field (<code class="mono">4.0 mm</code> default) and an amber tip whenever your plate is <code class="mono">&ge; 12 mm</code> (<code class="mono">1/2&Prime;</code>).</li>
              <li><strong>Clean Off-Plate Piercing:</strong> Your torch probes IHS on solid steel at the contour start and lifts to pierce height. It then shifts off the plate edge by the overhang distance, fires without blowback, and locks THC until traveling <code class="mono">6.0 mm</code> onto solid steel.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 2: Features table showing inline Center (On-Line) / Left / Right kerf selector and Edge-Start (Thick Plate) lead-in</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/v08-open-path-edge-start.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/v08-open-path-edge-start.png" alt="Step 2: Open-path Center Left Right kerf control and Edge-Start Thick Plate lead-in dropdown" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 3
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-3">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 03</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Remnant Skeleton Guillotine Crop Cuts (<code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Slice clean, square remnants off the back of your plate instead of cutting freehand by eye:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>In flat <span class="ui-chip">Stock Nesting</span>, open <span class="ui-chip">Guillotine Crop Cut</span> and choose <code class="mono">Best Single Cut</code>, <code class="mono">L-Cut (Both X &amp; Y)</code>, <code class="mono">Vertical (X)</code>, or <code class="mono">Horizontal (Y)</code>.</li>
              <li>Set the clearance margin (<code class="mono">kerf + 5.0 mm</code> default) to keep the shear line clear of your nested parts.</li>
              <li>Check the dashed <code class="mono">CROP</code> path(s) and highlighted <code class="mono">Usable Remnant</code> box with exact dimensions in the 2D Pack Part Preview before exporting G-code.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 3: Flat-sheet Pack Mode with Guillotine Crop Cut, Usable Remnant preview, and Chain/Bridge options</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/v08-flat-pro-pack.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/v08-flat-pro-pack.png" alt="Step 3: Flat-sheet Pack Mode showing Guillotine Crop Cut, Usable Remnant area, and Chain/Bridge cutting" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 4
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-4">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 04</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Serpentine <code class="mono">Daisy-Chain</code> &amp; <code class="mono">Micro-Bridge</code> Cutting (<code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Drop your pierce count per sheet, or keep small parts tied to the skeleton in one outer pass:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Load <span class="ui-chip cyan">Flat Chain &amp; Bridge</span> (<code class="mono">flat-chain-bridge-kit.svg</code>) from Quick CAD Fixtures to test on a multi-part plate.</li>
              <li>Uncheck <span class="ui-chip">Common-line cutting</span> first, since Chain/Bridge and Common-Line cannot run together.</li>
              <li>Pick <span class="ui-chip">Daisy-Chain (Single Pierce)</span> to link outer profiles in one continuous cut.</li>
              <li>Or pick <span class="ui-chip">Micro-Bridge (Connected)</span> to hold small parts with narrow uncut tabs. Interior holes always cut before the chained outer pass starts.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
{% endblock %}
